<!--
  Example mecatequi PR-body template.

  ACTIVATE: rename this file to `.github/mecatequi/pr-body.md` (drop the `.example`) and
  publish.sh will use it automatically — no workflow change needed. Or point the
  `MQ_PR_BODY_TEMPLATE` env var (see the Publish step) at any path relative to the checkout.

  The harness ALWAYS force-prepends the trust caveat
  ("⚠️ Agent-authored from the issue text — review carefully before merging.")
  above whatever this template renders, so you cannot accidentally drop the safety warning.
  Do NOT include your own ⚠️ caveat line in the template — it is prepended automatically;
  adding one yields a duplicate.

  Substitution is LITERAL and SINGLE-PASS: a {{placeholder}} below is replaced once with its
  value, the value is inserted verbatim (no shell/markdown interpretation), and an unknown
  {{token}} is left intact. Issue linkage is YOURS to control here — use {{issue_ref}} with
  `Closes`/`Refs` (the built-in default uses `Closes`).

  Available placeholders:
    {{what_agent_did}}  the model's own account of the change (final_text)
    {{files_changed}}   the name-status bullet list of changed files
    {{summary_table}}   the run-metadata markdown table
    {{run_url}}         link to the workflow run
    {{issue}}           the issue number, bare (e.g. 123)
    {{issue_ref}}       the issue reference (e.g. #123)
    {{stop_reason}}     the terminal stop reason
    {{non_empty_diff}}  whether the run left a diff (true/false)
    {{diff_bytes}}      size of the diff in bytes
    {{total_tokens}}    cumulative tokens for the run
    {{branch}}          the head branch the PR is opened from
    {{base}}            the base branch the PR targets
-->
## Summary

{{what_agent_did}}

## Changed files

{{files_changed}}

## Run details

{{summary_table}}

[View the workflow run]({{run_url}})

---
Closes {{issue_ref}}
